    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493308941/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Saturday, February 12, 1916, Ray’s, London
Alys went off at 8:35 from Euston. She is going to N.Y. second class on a second-class steamer! 
Eliza and I had a last row at the dressmaker’s over the bluse which cost £2.2 and is so badly made that I can hardly wear it. Lunched with Karin and said goodbye. 
Called on Mrs. Strong .  Went with Ray to see her Exhibition of Vanessa’s pictures, quite horrible. The MacLagans were there, full of disgust. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 50 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1916> .

